"gloss": "अमानिता f. (-ता) Modesty, humility.\n E. तल् added to अमानिन्, also with त्व,\nअमानित्वं.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "amanin": [{"id": "amAnin", "headword": "अमानिन्", "headword_slp1": "amAnin", "fold": "amanin", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Humble, modest.\n E. अ neg. मान pride, इनि\naffix. Also अमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं.)", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "amanusa": [{"id": "amAnuza", "headword": "अमानुष", "headword_slp1": "amAnuza", "fold": "amanusa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमानुष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Not human, animal, superhuman.\n E. अ neg. मानुष\nhuman.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अमानुषः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["amAnuzaH"]}], "amanya": [{"id": "amAnya", "headword": "अमान्य", "headword_slp1": "amAnya", "fold": "amanya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमान्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) To be disrespected.\n E. अ neg. मान्य to be respected.\nAlso अमाननीय and अमानितव्य.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अमान्यः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["amAnyaH"]}], "amamasi": [{"id": "amAmasI", "headword": "अमामसी", "headword_slp1": "amAmasI", "fold": "amamasi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमामसी f. (-सी) The day of new moon.\n E. अमा with, मस to measure, अच्\naffix, and ङीप् fem. do or with घञ् affix अमामासी.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "amavasi": [{"id": "amAvasI", "headword": "अमावसी", "headword_slp1": "amAvasI", "fold": "amavasi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमावसी f. (-सी) Day of new moon.\n E. अमा with, and वस to abide, अच्\naffix; being with, or in the same quarter as the sun; also अमावासी.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "amavasya": [{"id": "amAvAsya", "headword": "अमावास्य", "headword_slp1": "amAvAsya", "fold": "amavasya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमावास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Produced in the day of new moon.\n E. अमावास्या\nand अ aff.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "amAvAsyA", "headword": "अमावास्या", "headword_slp1": "amAvAsyA", "fold": "amavasya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमावास्या f. (-स्या) Day of conjunction or new moon.\n E. अमा with, (the\nsun and moon,) वस to abide, ण्यत् affix: or with the penult. vowel\nshort, अमावस्या; also अमावसी, &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "AmAvAsya", "headword": "आमावास्य", "headword_slp1": "AmAvAsya", "fold": "amavasya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "आमावास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Occurring on the day of conjunction, &c.\nE. अमावास्य and अञ् aff.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "amavasyaka": [{"id": "amAvAsyaka", "headword": "अमावास्यक", "headword_slp1": "amAvAsyaka", "fold": "amavasyaka", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमावास्यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Produced on the day of new moon. E.\nअमावास्या and वुन् aff.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "amaya": [{"id": "amAya", "headword": "अमाय", "headword_slp1": "amAya", "fold": "amaya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)\n 1. True, wise.\n 2. Sincere, guileless, free from error\nor deceit.\n f. (-या)\n 1. Absence of delusion, knowledge of the truth.\n2. Sincerity, honesty.\n E. अ neg. माया deceit, delusion.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "ammaya", "headword": "अम्मय", "headword_slp1": "ammaya", "fold": "amaya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अम्मय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Watery, formed from, or consisting of water, (as\nfroth, &c.)\n E. अप् water, and मयट् affix; प is changed to म, and the\nfem. takes ङीप्.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अम्मयं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ammayaM"]}, {"id": "Amaya", "headword": "आमय", "headword_slp1": "Amaya", "fold": "amaya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "आमय m. (-यः) Sickness, disease.\n n. (-यं) A grass, (Costus.)\n E. अम् to be\nsick, घञ् affix, आम, and य, from या to obtain.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आमयं", "आमयः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["AmayaM", "AmayaH"]}], "amayika": [{"id": "amAyika", "headword": "अमायिक", "headword_slp1": "amAyika", "fold": "amayika", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमायिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) True, real, honest, void of trick or guile.\n E. अ\nneg. मायिक deceptive.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अमायिकः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["amAyikaH"]}], "amayin": [{"id": "amAyin", "headword": "अमायिन्", "headword_slp1": "amAyin", "fold": "amayin", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Acting without illusion or deceit.\n E. अ neg.\nमायिन् deceitful.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "amarga": [{"id": "amArga", "headword": "अमार्ग", "headword_slp1": "amArga", "fold": "amarga", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमार्ग m. (-र्गः) Want of a road.\n mfn. (-र्गः-र्गा-र्गं) Without a road.\n E. अ neg.\nमार्ग a road.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अमार्गः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["amArgaH"]}], "amargita": [{"id": "amArgita", "headword": "अमार्गित", "headword_slp1": "amArgita", "fold": "amargita", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमार्गित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unsought, not hunted after.\n E. अ neg. मार्गित\nsought.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "amarjita": [{"id": "amArjjita", "headword": "अमार्ज्जित", "headword_slp1": "amArjjita", "fold": "amarjita", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "अमार्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)\n 1. Uncleansed.\n 2. Unadorned.\n E. अ neg. मार्ज्जित\ncleaned.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अमार्जित"], "synonyms_slp1": ["amArjita"]}], "amakumBa": [{"id": "AmakumBa", "headword": "आमकुम्भ", "headword_slp1": "AmakumBa", "fold": "amakumBa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "आमकुम्भ m. (-म्भः) A water-jar of unbaked clay.\n E. आम and कुम्भ a jar.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आमकुम्भः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["AmakumBaH"]}], "amaganDi": [{"id": "AmaganDi", "headword": "आमगन्धि", "headword_slp1": "AmaganDi", "fold": "amaganDi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "आमगन्धि n. (-न्धि) A bad and cadaverous smell, like that of raw meat\nor burning corpse.\n E. आम raw, &c. and गन्धि smell.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "amantraRa": [{"id": "AmantraRa", "headword": "आमन्त्रण", "headword_slp1": "AmantraRa", "fold": "amantraRa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "आमन्त्रण nf. (-णं-णा)\n 1. Calling or calling to.\n 2. Courtesy, welcome, adieu,\n&c.\n 3. Inviting, invitation.\n 4. Interrogation.\n 5. The vocative case.\nE. आङ् before मत्रि to consult, affix युच्.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आमंत्रणं", "आमन्त्रणं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["AmaMtraRaM", "AmantraRaM"]}], "amantrayitf": [{"id": "Amantrayitf", "headword": "आमन्त्रयितृ", "headword_slp1": "Amantrayitf", "fold": "amantrayitf", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "आमन्त्रयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Asking, inviting, calling.\n m. (-ता) An inviter,\nan entertainer, especially of Brahmans.\n E. आङ् before मत्रि to\ncounsel, causal form, तृच् aff.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आमंत्रयितृ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["AmaMtrayitf"]}], "amantrita": [{"id": "Amantrita", "headword": "आमन्त्रित", "headword_slp1": "Amantrita", "fold": "amantrita", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "shabda-sagara", "senses": [{"gloss": "आमन्त्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Invited, summoned, called.\n E. आङ् before मत्रि to\nconsult, क्त aff.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आमंत्रित"], "synonyms_slp1": ["AmaMtrita"]}], "amapinasa": [{"id": "A